MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The SanDisk 32GB card fits my repeated use of SD and microSD storage, adapters, card holders, and a reader; it serves an ongoing practical need across my devices.",
    "The Fire TV Sticks offer a useful way to add streaming to my Samsung TV. I would choose one, although my 720p screen gives me no reason to prioritize 4K."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Echo speakers and smart display introduce voice-assistant uses I have not been looking for; they do not help with the storage, charging, mounting, and camera accessories I regularly choose.",
    "An older Fire tablet duplicates the Fire 7 I already have, while the keyboard, earbuds, and Bluetooth speaker solve needs I do not currently have. Being usable with electronics is not enough to make them useful purchases now."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My Fire tablet purchase seems to have been taken as interest in a broad range of Amazon devices, even though owning a tablet does not make me want Alexa speakers or another tablet.",
    "My TV and device purchases seem to have been stretched into general interest in entertainment electronics, when most of my choices are specific accessories with a clear practical purpose."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "I repeatedly choose items that support equipment I already use: memory cards, cables, mounts, power strips, and camera accessories. Compatibility and the job an item performs matter more to me than a shared brand.",
    "Ownership changes what I need next: my existing tablet makes another older tablet less useful, and the two Fire TV Sticks are alternatives for one streaming need rather than two separate purchases."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You recognized my storage and TV connectivity interests, but stretched my device ownership into interest in extra gadgets without a current practical use."
}
